  "summary_text": "Beacon Freight\nSSO will ship with the Teams launch\nBeacon Freight asked about EU data residency\nReporting export and edge cases and trial period\nReporting export and email digests seen as one underlying problem\nEdge cases is on the critical path\nEdge cases is the scary part\nConcern with trial period: that it just sits there\nTrial period is the blocker\nPreference to document the decision rather than split it into two pieces\nChampion on their side and spreadsheet and sandbox account\nReal issue may be action items rather than champion on their side\nChampion on their side is kind of a mystery\nSpreadsheet is not urgent\nSandbox account is good enough for now\nPreference to cut the scope rather than check with legal\nFeedback from their managers and change management piece and scope\nFeedback from their managers is way more complicated than it looks\nFeedback from their managers is sort of on hold\nChange management piece is sort of on hold\nScope is fine in theory\nIntegration with their hr system and onboarding calls and doc\nFeedback on integration with their hr system from the design team: they were pretty chill about it\nOnboarding calls is way more complicated than it looks\nConcern with doc: that we're solving the wrong problem\nFollow ups and dependencies and pilot group\nFollow ups is still pretty rough\nFeedback on dependencies from people on the other team: they were surprised\nPilot group is unclear",
  "summary_markdown": "### Beacon Freight\n- SSO will ship with the Teams launch\n- Beacon Freight asked about EU data residency\n\n### Reporting export and edge cases and trial period\n- Reporting export and email digests seen as one underlying problem\n- Edge cases is on the critical path\n  - Edge cases is the scary part\n- Concern with trial period: that it just sits there\n  - Trial period is the blocker\n- Preference to document the decision rather than split it into two pieces\n\n### Champion on their side and spreadsheet and sandbox account\n- Real issue may be action items rather than champion on their side\n  - Champion on their side is kind of a mystery\n- Spreadsheet is not urgent\n- Sandbox account is good enough for now\n- Preference to cut the scope rather than check with legal\n\n### Feedback from their managers and change management piece and scope\n- Feedback from their managers is way more complicated than it looks\n  - Feedback from their managers is sort of on hold\n- Change management piece is sort of on hold\n- Scope is fine in theory\n\n### Integration with their hr system and onboarding calls and doc\n- Feedback on integration with their hr system from the design team: they were pretty chill about it\n- Onboarding calls is way more complicated than it looks\n- Concern with doc: that we're solving the wrong problem\n\n### Follow ups and dependencies and pilot group\n- Follow ups is still pretty rough\n- Feedback on dependencies from people on the other team: they were surprised\n- Pilot group is unclear",
  "private_notes_text": null,
  "private_notes_markdown": null,
  "transcript": [
    {
